<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrītābĭlis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ), e,
			adj.
		1. irrito. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Easily excited</i> or <i>enraged</i>,
				<i>irritable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irritabiles esse animos optimorum saepe
					hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 17, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus vatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 102</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Amm. 18, 6, 18</span></i>.—
			* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>easily exciting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 6, 23, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
